course: dictionary
lesson: 6264
title: Moment: a short time, or one exact point
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A moment is a very short time. «Wait a moment» means wait a little, not for an hour. The words around the word give the clue.
explain: A moment can also be one exact point in time. In «Charles became King the moment his mother died», the words «the moment» tell you exactly when it happened.
explain: Some moments are not about the clock at all. A proud moment or a big moment is an important time, like the day you read your first whole book.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. In «Wait a moment», if you swap in «wait a little», the sentence still makes sense, so you know you have it right.
fact: A moment is a very short time, or one exact point in time.
fact: «Wait a moment» means wait a little.
fact: «In a moment» means soon, and «for the moment» means for now.
fact: «At that moment» points to one exact point in the story.
fact: A big moment or a proud moment is an important time in your life.
exercise: «Shout hello in a big empty hall and a moment later the walls shout it back.» How long is a moment here? | Never | *A very short time | A whole day | A whole year
exercise: Ben says «I will be there in a moment» means never. What does it really mean? | Never | Very loudly | *Soon | Last year
exercise: «Charles became King the moment his mother died.» What does moment point to here? | A holiday | *The exact point when his mother died | A map | A long, slow time
test: «It was a proud moment when Maya read her first whole book.» What kind of moment is this? | A problem | A time on a clock | *An important time in her life | A few seconds only
test: «For the moment, the cat is asleep.» What does for the moment mean? | Forever | *For now | Very loudly | Last week
exam: Which use of moment means a very short time? | «At that moment the bell rang.» | *«Wait a moment, please.» | «A big moment for the team.»
